IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea2-part-9a`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 9, SECTIONS 81 TO 87
-- (maternity: no dismissal during the absence, the employer's offences, the right to
-- the payment when a notice of dismissal is given, contracting out, penalties).  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * Months are counted with daydate `add months`, which clamps the day to the end of a short
--     month (31 August less 6 months is 28 February).  The Act has no rule for counting months
--     from a day (the staged Interpretation Act module says so); fork F6 in NOTES.md.
--   * "within a period of N months preceding D" is read as the days from D less N months up to
--     the day before D (fork F7).
--   * Entitlement answers (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) are used as in ea2-part-9a.

§ `Part 9 -- no notice of dismissal during the absence, and the offence of employing her (ss 81 to 83)`

-- s 81: "when a female employee absents herself from work in accordance with the provisions of this
-- Part it is not lawful for her employer to give her notice of dismissal during her absence or on
-- such a day that the notice will expire during her absence."  Only a notice her employer gives.
-- src:2996 | 81. Without affecting sections 84 and 84A, when a female
-- src:2997 | employee absents herself from work in accordance with the
-- src:2998 | provisions of this Part it is not lawful for her employer to give her
-- src:2999 | notice of dismissal during her absence or on such a day that the notice
-- src:3000 | will expire during her absence.
@ref s 81 (src:2996-3000)
GIVEN `she absents herself from work in accordance with the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of her absence` IS A `Period of days`
      notice IS A `Notice of termination`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 it is lawful for her employer to give her the notice of dismissal` MEANS
    IF `she absents herself from work in accordance with the provisions of this Part`
       AND notice's `given by` EQUALS `Party who is the employer`
       AND (    (notice's `given on` AT LEAST `the period of her absence`'s `first day`
                 AND notice's `given on` AT MOST `the period of her absence`'s `last day`)
            OR  (notice's `last day of the notice` AT LEAST `the period of her absence`'s `first day`
                 AND notice's `last day of the notice` AT MOST `the period of her absence`'s `last day`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not lawful for her employer to give her notice of dismissal"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section never says that a notice is lawful, so the case outside its "when" and outside her absence is answered by the twin `s 81 it is not lawful for her employer to give her the notice of dismissal` below
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The twin that asks the text's own question, with the text's own words ("it is not lawful").  The text
-- gives its "when" and the period "during her absence or on such a day that the notice will expire
-- during her absence" in its own words, so a case outside either is the text's no (rulings (b) and
-- (a) of 2026-11-05, "when" counting as "where"; fork F18).
-- src:2996 | 81. Without affecting sections 84 and 84A, when a female
-- src:2997 | employee absents herself from work in accordance with the
-- src:2998 | provisions of this Part it is not lawful for her employer to give her
-- src:2999 | notice of dismissal during her absence or on such a day that the notice
-- src:3000 | will expire during her absence.
@ref s 81 (src:2996-3000)
GIVEN `she absents herself from work in accordance with the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of her absence` IS A `Period of days`
      notice IS A `Notice of termination`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 it is not lawful for her employer to give her the notice of dismissal` MEANS
    IF `she absents herself from work in accordance with the provisions of this Part`
       AND notice's `given by` EQUALS `Party who is the employer`
       AND (    (notice's `given on` AT LEAST `the period of her absence`'s `first day`
                 AND notice's `given on` AT MOST `the period of her absence`'s `last day`)
            OR  (notice's `last day of the notice` AT LEAST `the period of her absence`'s `first day`
                 AND notice's `last day of the notice` AT MOST `the period of her absence`'s `last day`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a female employee absents herself from work in accordance with the provisions of this Part"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 82: "Any employer who knowingly employs a female employee at any time during the period of 4 weeks
-- immediately following her confinement shall be guilty of an offence."  The 4 weeks (28 days) begin
-- on the day of the confinement, the same placement as the 8 weeks of s 76(1)(a)(ii) (fork F1).
-- src:3004 | 82. Any employer who knowingly employs a female employee at
-- src:3005 | any time during the period of 4 weeks immediately following her
-- src:3006 | confinement shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 82 (src:3004-3006)
GIVEN `the employer knowingly employed her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the employer employed her` IS A DATE
      `the day of her confinement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82 the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the day the employer employed her` LESS THAN `the day of her confinement`
       OR `the day the employer employed her` GREATER THAN `the day of her confinement` PLUS 27
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the period of 4 weeks immediately following her confinement"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        IF `the employer knowingly employed her`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of an employer "who knowingly employs"; the section says nothing of an employer who did not know
        ELSE NOTHING

-- s 83: "If a female employee works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work
-- under the provisions of this Part, she forfeits her claim to any payment to which she is entitled
-- under this Part and is liable to dismissal."
-- src:3010 | 83. If a female employee works for any other employer after she has
-- src:3011 | absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part, she
-- src:3012 | forfeits her claim to any payment to which she is entitled under this
-- src:3013 | Part and is liable to dismissal.
@ref s 83 (src:3010-3013)
GIVEN `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83 the female employee keeps her claim to payment under this Part` MEANS
    IF `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "she forfeits her claim to any payment"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section never says she keeps her claim, so the case outside its "If" is answered by the twin `s 83 the female employee forfeits her claim to payment under this Part` below
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3010 | 83. If a female employee works for any other employer after she has
-- src:3011 | absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part, she
-- src:3012 | forfeits her claim to any payment to which she is entitled under this
-- src:3013 | Part and is liable to dismissal.
@ref s 83 (src:3010-3013)
GIVEN `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83 the female employee forfeits her claim to payment under this Part` MEANS
    IF `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a female employee works for any other employer after she has absented herself"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3010 | 83. If a female employee works for any other employer after she has
-- src:3011 | absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part, she
-- src:3012 | forfeits her claim to any payment to which she is entitled under this
-- src:3013 | Part and is liable to dismissal.
@ref s 83 (src:3010-3013)
GIVEN `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83 the female employee is liable to dismissal` MEANS
    IF `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a female employee works for any other employer after she has absented herself"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 83 (src:3010-3013)
GIVEN `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83 the employer may dismiss the female employee` MEANS
    IF `she works for any other employer after she has absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section never says the employer may not dismiss her on any other ground; the twin `s 83 the female employee is liable to dismissal` above asks the text's own question
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 9 -- a notice of dismissal does not take away the payment (ss 84 and 84A)`

-- A helper for ss 84 and 84A: the day falls in the N months before the date, from the date less N
-- months to the day before the date (fork F7).
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      date IS A DATE
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) helper: the day is within the months preceding the date` MEANS
    day AT LEAST `add months` date (0 MINUS months) AND day LESS THAN date

-- A helper for ss 84 and 84A: limb (a) or limb (c) in the words of the section: the notice was given
-- within the N months preceding the estimated delivery date, or within the N months preceding the date of
-- her confinement.
GIVEN `the day the notice of dismissal was given` IS A DATE
      `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of her confinement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) helper: the notice was given within the months preceding the estimated delivery date or the confinement` MEANS
    (CONSIDER `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner`
     WHEN JUST estimated THEN `s 84(1) helper: the day is within the months preceding the date` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` estimated months
     WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    OR
    (CONSIDER `the day of her confinement`
     WHEN JUST confined THEN `s 84(1) helper: the day is within the months preceding the date` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` confined months
     WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

-- s 84(1): a notice of dismissal given without sufficient cause by an employer to a female employee
-- which (a) before 1 May 2013 is given within 6 months before the estimated delivery date or the
-- confinement; (b) on or after 1 May 2013 is given at any time of her pregnancy (certified before the
-- notice is given) where she has served the employer 3 months or more; (c) on or after 1 May 2013 but
-- before 1 August 2013, where she has served less than 3 months, is given within 6 months before the
-- estimated delivery date or the confinement -- "does not have the effect of depriving her of any
-- payment" under this Part.
-- src:3021 | 84.—(1) Without affecting sections 81 and 84A, a notice of
-- src:3022 | dismissal given without sufficient cause by an employer to a
-- src:3023 | female employee which —
-- src:3025 | (a) if given before 1 May 2013, is given —
-- src:3027 | (i) within a period of 6 months preceding the estimated
-- src:3028 | delivery date for her confinement (as certified by a
-- src:3029 | medical practitioner); or
-- src:3031 | (ii) within a period of 6 months preceding the date of her
-- src:3032 | confinement;
-- src:3034 | (b) if given on or after 1 May 2013, is given at any time of her
-- src:3035 | pregnancy (as certified by a medical practitioner before the
-- src:3036 | notice of dismissal is given), where the female employee
-- src:3037 | has served the employer for a period of 3 months or more
-- src:3038 | immediately preceding the day the notice is given; or
-- src:3040 | (c) if given on or after 1 May 2013 but before 1 August 2013
-- src:3041 | and where the female employee has served the employer
-- src:3042 | for a period of less than 3 months, is given —
-- src:3044 | (i) within a period of 6 months preceding the estimated
-- src:3045 | delivery date for her confinement (as certified by a
-- src:3046 | medical practitioner); or
-- src:3048 | (ii) within a period of 6 months preceding the date of her
-- src:3049 | confinement,
-- src:3051 | does not have the effect of depriving her of any payment to which, but
-- src:3052 | for that notice, she would have been entitled or would, on or before
-- src:3053 | the date of her confinement, have become entitled to under this Part.
@ref s 84(1) (src:3021-3053)
GIVEN `the notice of dismissal was given without sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice of dismissal was given` IS A DATE
      `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of her confinement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `her pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the completed months she had served the employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) the notice of dismissal has the effect of depriving her of a payment under this Part` MEANS
    IF `the notice of dismissal was given without sufficient cause`
       AND (    (`the day the notice of dismissal was given` LESS THAN (Date 1 5 2013)
                 AND `s 84(1) helper: the notice was given within the months preceding the estimated delivery date or the confinement` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner` `the day of her confinement` 6)
            OR  (`the day the notice of dismissal was given` AT LEAST (Date 1 5 2013)
                 AND `her pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given`
                 AND `the completed months she had served the employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` AT LEAST 3)
            OR  (`the day the notice of dismissal was given` AT LEAST (Date 1 5 2013)
                 AND `the day the notice of dismissal was given` LESS THAN (Date 1 8 2013)
                 AND `the completed months she had served the employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` LESS THAN 3
                 AND `s 84(1) helper: the notice was given within the months preceding the estimated delivery date or the confinement` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner` `the day of her confinement` 6))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not have the effect of depriving her of any payment"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section protects a notice given without sufficient cause in one of the three circumstances of paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- A record: one estimated delivery date and the day a medical practitioner certified it.
DECLARE `s 84(1A) Certified estimated delivery date` HAS
    `the estimated delivery date` IS A DATE
    `the day it was certified` IS A DATE

-- A helper: the latest day, before the notice, on which a certification was made (NOTHING if none).
GIVEN `the day the notice of dismissal is given` IS A DATE
      certified IS A LIST OF `s 84(1A) Certified estimated delivery date`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 84(1A) helper: the latest day of certification before the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER certified
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only an estimated delivery date certified before the notice of dismissal is given can be the relevant one, and none is listed
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `s 84(1A) helper: the latest day of certification before the notice` `the day the notice of dismissal is given` rest
        WHEN JUST later THEN
            IF c's `the day it was certified` LESS THAN `the day the notice of dismissal is given` AND c's `the day it was certified` GREATER THAN later
            THEN JUST (c's `the day it was certified`)
            ELSE JUST later
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF c's `the day it was certified` LESS THAN `the day the notice of dismissal is given`
            THEN JUST (c's `the day it was certified`)
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only an estimated delivery date certified before the notice of dismissal is given can be the relevant one
            ELSE NOTHING

-- A helper: the estimated delivery dates certified on that day.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      certified IS A LIST OF `s 84(1A) Certified estimated delivery date`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`s 84(1A) helper: the estimated delivery dates certified on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER certified
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF c's `the day it was certified` EQUALS day
        THEN c's `the estimated delivery date` FOLLOWED BY `s 84(1A) helper: the estimated delivery dates certified on the day` day rest
        ELSE `s 84(1A) helper: the estimated delivery dates certified on the day` day rest

-- A helper: all the dates in a list are the same date (so the list names one date).
GIVEN dates IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 84(1A) helper: the one date the list names` MEANS
    CONSIDER dates
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no estimated delivery date was certified on that day
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `s 84(1A) helper: every date in the list is` d rest
        THEN JUST d
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Act does not choose between two different estimated delivery dates certified on the same closest day
        ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      dates IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(1A) helper: every date in the list is` MEANS
    CONSIDER dates
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x EQUALS d AND `s 84(1A) helper: every date in the list is` d rest

-- s 84(1A): "In any case where there are 2 or more estimated delivery dates (each certified by a medical
-- practitioner) ..., the estimated delivery date that is relevant ... is the estimated delivery date
-- (a) which is certified by a medical practitioner before the notice of dismissal is given by her
-- employer; and (b) the date of such certification of which is closest to the date the notice of
-- dismissal is given."  If two different dates were certified on the same closest day, the Act does not choose.
-- src:3057 | (1A) In any case where there are 2 or more estimated delivery dates
-- src:3058 | (each certified by a medical practitioner) for the confinement of a
-- src:3059 | female employee, the estimated delivery date that is relevant for the
-- src:3060 | purposes of subsection (1) is the estimated delivery date —
-- src:3062 | (a) which is certified by a medical practitioner before the
-- src:3063 | notice of dismissal is given by her employer; and
-- src:3068 | (b) the date of such certification of which is closest to the date
-- src:3069 | the notice of dismissal is given.
@ref s 84(1A) (src:3057-3069)
GIVEN `the day the notice of dismissal is given` IS A DATE
      certified IS A LIST OF `s 84(1A) Certified estimated delivery date`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 84(1A) the estimated delivery date that is relevant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 84(1A) helper: the latest day of certification before the notice` `the day the notice of dismissal is given` certified
    WHEN JUST latest THEN
        `s 84(1A) helper: the one date the list names` (`s 84(1A) helper: the estimated delivery dates certified on the day` latest certified)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only an estimated delivery date certified before the notice of dismissal is given can be the relevant one, and there is none
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 84(2): "Subject to section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016, where a female employee in the
-- circumstances mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) considers that a notice of dismissal given to
-- her was not given for sufficient cause, the female employee may lodge a claim, under section 13 of that
-- Act, for either of the following remedies: (a) reinstatement ...; (b) compensation."
-- src:3071 | (2) Subject to section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016, where
-- src:3072 | a female employee in the circumstances mentioned in
-- src:3073 | subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) considers that a notice of dismissal
-- src:3074 | given to her was not given for sufficient cause, the female employee
-- src:3075 | may lodge a claim, under section 13 of that Act, for either of the
-- src:3076 | following remedies:
-- src:3078 | (a) reinstatement in her former employment;
-- src:3080 | (b) compensation.
@ref s 84(2) (src:3071-3080)
GIVEN `she is in the circumstances mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she considers that the notice of dismissal was not given for sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 allows the claim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      relief IS A `Relief a claimant may seek`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(2) the female employee may lodge a claim for the relief` MEANS
    IF NOT (`she is in the circumstances mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)`
            AND `she considers that the notice of dismissal was not given for sufficient cause`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a female employee in the circumstances mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) considers"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        IF `section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 allows the claim` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN
            CONSIDER relief
            WHEN `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `Relief: compensation` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names "either of the following remedies" and does not say whether any other relief may be claimed under it
            WHEN `Relief: payment of a sum the Commissioner considers just` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the claim is "Subject to section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016", which is not among the sources and does not allow it here
        ELSE NOTHING

-- s 84(3)(a): "If a Tribunal hearing the claim is satisfied that the female employee has been dismissed
-- without sufficient cause, the Tribunal may, despite any rule of law or agreement to the contrary --
-- (a) in a claim for reinstatement ..., direct the employer (i) to reinstate the employee ...; and
-- (ii) to pay the employee an amount equivalent to the wages that the employee would have earned".
-- src:3084 | (3) If a Tribunal hearing the claim is satisfied that the female
-- src:3085 | employee has been dismissed without sufficient cause, the Tribunal
-- src:3086 | may, despite any rule of law or agreement to the contrary —
-- src:3088 | (a) in a claim for reinstatement of the employee in her former
-- src:3089 | employment, direct the employer —
-- src:3091 | (i) to reinstate the employee in her former employment;
-- src:3092 | and
-- src:3094 | (ii) to pay the employee an amount equivalent to the
-- src:3095 | wages that the employee would have earned, if she
-- src:3096 | had not been dismissed by the employer; or
@ref s 84(3)(a) (src:3084-3096)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "Tribunal"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claim is for reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that she has been dismissed without sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate her and to pay her the wages she would have earned` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 2(1) "Tribunal"`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT `the claim is for reinstatement`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) is for "a claim for reinstatement"
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE
            IF `the Tribunal is satisfied that she has been dismissed without sufficient cause`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a Tribunal hearing the claim is satisfied that the female employee has been dismissed without sufficient cause"
            ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is the power of "a Tribunal hearing the claim", and the body is not one
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is the Tribunal is the answer of s 2(1) "Tribunal", which the Act did not give on these facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 84(3)(b): "in a claim for compensation, direct the employer to pay, as compensation to the employee,
-- an amount of wages determined by the Tribunal to be just and equitable having regard to all the
-- circumstances of the case."
-- src:3098 | (b) in a claim for compensation, direct the employer to pay, as
-- src:3099 | compensation to the employee, an amount of wages
-- src:3100 | determined by the Tribunal to be just and equitable
-- src:3101 | having regard to all the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 84(3)(b) (src:3098-3101)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "Tribunal"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claim is for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that she has been dismissed without sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(3)(b) the Tribunal may direct the employer to pay her compensation in wages` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 2(1) "Tribunal"`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT `the claim is for compensation`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) is for "a claim for compensation"
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE
            IF `the Tribunal is satisfied that she has been dismissed without sufficient cause`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a Tribunal hearing the claim is satisfied that the female employee has been dismissed without sufficient cause"
            ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is the power of "a Tribunal hearing the claim", and the body is not one
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is the Tribunal is the answer of s 2(1) "Tribunal", which the Act did not give on these facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 84A(1): the same protection for a notice of dismissal given on the ground of redundancy or by
-- reason of reorganisation, with 3 months in place of 6.
-- src:3109 | 84A.—(1) Without affecting sections 81 and 84, a notice of
-- src:3110 | dismissal given to a female employee by her employer on the
-- src:3111 | ground of redundancy or by reason of any reorganisation of her
-- src:3112 | employer’s profession, business, trade or work —
-- src:3117 | (a) if given before 1 May 2013, is given —
-- src:3119 | (i) within a period of 3 months preceding the estimated
-- src:3120 | delivery date for her confinement (as certified by a
-- src:3121 | medical practitioner); or
-- src:3123 | (ii) within a period of 3 months preceding the date of her
-- src:3124 | confinement;
-- src:3126 | (b) if given on or after 1 May 2013, is given at any time of her
-- src:3127 | pregnancy (as certified by a medical practitioner before the
-- src:3128 | notice of dismissal is given), where the female employee
-- src:3129 | has served the employer for a period of 3 months or more
-- src:3130 | immediately preceding the day the notice is given; or
-- src:3132 | (c) if given on or after 1 May 2013 but before 1 August 2013
-- src:3133 | and where the female employee has served the employer
-- src:3134 | for a period of less than 3 months, is given —
-- src:3136 | (i) within a period of 3 months preceding the estimated
-- src:3137 | delivery date for her confinement (as certified by a
-- src:3138 | medical practitioner); or
-- src:3140 | (ii) within a period of 3 months preceding the date of her
-- src:3141 | confinement,
-- src:3143 | does not have the effect of depriving her of any payment to which, but
-- src:3144 | for that notice, she would have been entitled or would, on or before
-- src:3145 | the date of her confinement, have become entitled to under this Part.
@ref s 84A(1) (src:3109-3145)
GIVEN `the notice of dismissal was given on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation of her employer's profession, business, trade or work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice of dismissal was given` IS A DATE
      `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of her confinement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `her pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the completed months she had served the employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84A(1) the notice of dismissal has the effect of depriving her of a payment under this Part` MEANS
    IF `the notice of dismissal was given on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation of her employer's profession, business, trade or work`
       AND (    (`the day the notice of dismissal was given` LESS THAN (Date 1 5 2013)
                 AND `s 84(1) helper: the notice was given within the months preceding the estimated delivery date or the confinement` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner` `the day of her confinement` 3)
            OR  (`the day the notice of dismissal was given` AT LEAST (Date 1 5 2013)
                 AND `her pregnancy was certified by a medical practitioner before the notice was given`
                 AND `the completed months she had served the employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` AT LEAST 3)
            OR  (`the day the notice of dismissal was given` AT LEAST (Date 1 5 2013)
                 AND `the day the notice of dismissal was given` LESS THAN (Date 1 8 2013)
                 AND `the completed months she had served the employer immediately preceding the day the notice was given` LESS THAN 3
                 AND `s 84(1) helper: the notice was given within the months preceding the estimated delivery date or the confinement` `the day the notice of dismissal was given` `the estimated delivery date certified by a medical practitioner` `the day of her confinement` 3))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not have the effect of depriving her of any payment"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section protects a notice given on the ground of redundancy or reorganisation in one of the three circumstances of paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 84A(2): the relevant estimated delivery date, the same rule as s 84(1A), word for word.
-- src:3149 | (2) In any case where there are 2 or more estimated delivery dates
-- src:3150 | (each certified by a medical practitioner) for the confinement of a
-- src:3151 | female employee, the estimated delivery date that is relevant for the
-- src:3152 | purposes of subsection (1) is the estimated delivery date —
-- src:3154 | (a) which is certified by a medical practitioner before the
-- src:3155 | notice of dismissal is given by her employer; and
-- src:3157 | (b) the date of such certification of which is closest to the date
-- src:3158 | the notice of dismissal is given.
@ref s 84A(2) (src:3149-3158)
GIVEN `the day the notice of dismissal is given` IS A DATE
      certified IS A LIST OF `s 84(1A) Certified estimated delivery date`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 84A(2) the estimated delivery date that is relevant` MEANS
    `s 84(1A) the estimated delivery date that is relevant` `the day the notice of dismissal is given` certified

-- s 84A(3): "The payment referred to in subsection (1) is in addition to any retrenchment benefit or
-- other payment to which the female employee is entitled under the terms of her contract of service or
-- under any other written law."
-- src:3160 | (3) The payment referred to in subsection (1) is in addition to any
-- src:3161 | retrenchment benefit or other payment to which the female employee
-- src:3166 | is entitled under the terms of her contract of service or under any other
-- src:3167 | written law.
@ref s 84A(3) (src:3160-3167)
GIVEN `the payment is a payment referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84A(3) the payment is in addition to a retrenchment benefit or other payment` MEANS
    IF `the payment is a payment referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of "The payment referred to in subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 9 -- contracting out, and the offences and penalties (ss 86 and 87)`

-- s 86: a term of a contract of service by which a female employee relinquishes any right to maternity
-- benefit under this Part "is void insofar as it purports to deprive her of that right or to remove or
-- reduce the liability of any employer to make any payment under this Part".
-- src:3173 | 86. Any contract of service whereby a female employee
-- src:3174 | relinquishes any right to maternity benefit under this Part is void
-- src:3175 | insofar as it purports to deprive her of that right or to remove or
-- src:3176 | reduce the liability of any employer to make any payment under this
-- src:3177 | Part.
@ref s 86 (src:3173-3177)
GIVEN `it is a term of a contract of service by which a female employee relinquishes a right to maternity benefit under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term purports to deprive her of that right or to remove or reduce the liability of an employer to make a payment under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 the term of the contract of service is void` MEANS
    IF `it is a term of a contract of service by which a female employee relinquishes a right to maternity benefit under this Part`
       AND `the term purports to deprive her of that right or to remove or reduce the liability of an employer to make a payment under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the contract is void only "insofar as it purports to deprive her of that right or to remove or reduce the liability of any employer"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 87(1): an employer who (a) fails, without reasonable cause, to grant maternity leave under this Part
-- to a female employee who is entitled to and requests it; (b) fails to pay the employer's female
-- employee in accordance with any provision of this Part (other than s 87A); or (c) acts in
-- contravention of s 81 "shall be guilty of an offence".
-- src:3181 | 87.—(1) Any employer who —
-- src:3183 | (a) fails, without reasonable cause, to grant maternity leave
-- src:3184 | under this Part to a female employee who is entitled to and
-- src:3185 | requests for the leave;
-- src:3187 | (b) fails to pay the employer’s female employee in accordance
-- src:3188 | with any of the provisions of this Part (other than
-- src:3189 | section 87A); or
-- src:3191 | (c) acts in contravention of section 81,
-- src:3193 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:3194 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:3195 | 6 months or to both.
@ref s 87(1) (src:3181-3195)
GIVEN `the employer failed, without reasonable cause, to grant maternity leave under this Part to a female employee who is entitled to it and requests it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer failed to pay the employer's female employee in accordance with a provision of this Part other than section 87A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer acted in contravention of section 81` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer failed, without reasonable cause, to grant maternity leave under this Part to a female employee who is entitled to it and requests it`
       OR `the employer failed to pay the employer's female employee in accordance with a provision of this Part other than section 87A`
       OR `the employer acted in contravention of section 81`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is the failure in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 87(1): the penalty on conviction: a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 6 months or both.
@ref s 87(1) (src:3181-3195)
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 87(1) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- s 87(2): "Any employer who is guilty of an offence under section 82 shall be liable on conviction to
-- a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both."
-- src:3199 | (2) Any employer who is guilty of an offence under section 82 shall
-- src:3200 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to
-- src:3201 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref s 87(2) (src:3199-3201)
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 87(2) the penalty on conviction for an offence under section 82` MEANS
    `Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- s 87(3): a repeat offender "shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both".
-- src:3205 | (3) Where an employer who is convicted or found guilty of an
-- src:3206 | offence under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) or section 82 is a repeat
-- src:3207 | offender, the employer shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3208 | exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:3209 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 87(3) (src:3205-3209)
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 87(3) the penalty on conviction of a repeat offender` MEANS
    `Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 10000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12

-- The kind of an earlier conviction, for s 87(4).
DECLARE `s 87(4) Kind of earlier conviction` IS ONE OF
    `s 87(4)(a) an offence under section 87(1)(a), (b) or (c) or section 82`
    `s 87(4)(b) an offence under section 17(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001`
    `s 87(4) an offence of some other kind`

DECLARE `s 87(4) Earlier conviction` HAS
    `kind of offence` IS A `s 87(4) Kind of earlier conviction`
    `the day the person was convicted or found guilty` IS A DATE

-- A helper: how many of the earlier convictions are of a kind in paragraph (a) or (b), on or after
-- 1 May 2013 and before the day of the current conviction.
GIVEN `the day of the current conviction` IS A DATE
      earlier IS A LIST OF `s 87(4) Earlier conviction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 87(4) helper: the earlier convictions that count` MEANS
    CONSIDER earlier
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF (e's `kind of offence` EQUALS `s 87(4)(a) an offence under section 87(1)(a), (b) or (c) or section 82`
             OR e's `kind of offence` EQUALS `s 87(4)(b) an offence under section 17(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001`)
            AND e's `the day the person was convicted or found guilty` AT LEAST (Date 1 5 2013)
            AND e's `the day the person was convicted or found guilty` LESS THAN `the day of the current conviction`
         THEN 1
         ELSE 0)
        PLUS `s 87(4) helper: the earlier convictions that count` `the day of the current conviction` rest

-- s 87(4): "a person is a repeat offender ... if the person ... has been convicted or found guilty of (a)
-- an offence under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) or section 82; or (b) an offence under section 17(1) of
-- the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 ..., on at least one other occasion on or after 1 May 2013
-- and before the date on which the person is convicted ... of the current offence."  Each earlier
-- conviction in the list is one occasion.
-- src:3216 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a person is a repeat offender
-- src:3217 | in relation to an offence under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) or
-- src:3218 | section 82 if the person who is convicted or found guilty of an offence
-- src:3219 | under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) or section 82 (called the current
-- src:3220 | offence) has been convicted or found guilty of —
-- src:3222 | (a) an offence under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) or section 82;
-- src:3223 | or
-- src:3225 | (b) an offence under section 17(1) of the Child Development
-- src:3226 | Co‑Savings Act 2001 in force before, on or after 1 May
-- src:3227 | 2013,
-- src:3229 | on at least one other occasion on or after 1 May 2013 and before the
-- src:3230 | date on which the person is convicted or found guilty of the current
-- src:3231 | offence.
@ref s 87(4) (src:3216-3231)
GIVEN `the day of the current conviction` IS A DATE
      earlier IS A LIST OF `s 87(4) Earlier conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(4) the person is a repeat offender` MEANS
    IF `s 87(4) helper: the earlier convictions that count` `the day of the current conviction` earlier AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is a repeat offender in relation to an offence under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) or section 82 if"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Part 9 -- the payment is gathered from the sections that give and take it away (E1 option B, by hand)`

-- E1 (Meng, 2026-11-04): option C, each section answers on its own, is what ss 76 to 84 do.  This
-- one rule gathers, by hand and in plain L4, the answers that decide whether the female employee is
-- paid for the benefit period, so that a reader (and the seat layer) has one place to look.  It adds
-- no rule: a section that says she is not entitled (or forfeits) wins; otherwise s 76(1A)'s grant
-- decides; if the sections do not answer it is NOTHING.  Fork F8 in NOTES.md.
-- src:2807 | (1A) Subject to this section and section 77, every female employee
-- src:2808 | is entitled to receive payment from her employer at her gross rate of
-- src:2809 | pay for any of the following periods (called in this Part the benefit
-- src:2810 | period):
@ref s 76(1A) (src:2807-2810)
GIVEN `the answer of s 76(1A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 76(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 76(2A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 76(2B)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 76(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 76(5A)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 83` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1A) gathered with ss 76(2) to (5A) and 83: the female employee is entitled to payment for the benefit period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period"
        IF `the answer of s 76(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period"
        IF `the answer of s 76(2A)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period"
        IF `the answer of s 76(2B)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any payment under subsection (1A) for any confinement"
        IF `the answer of s 76(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "she forfeits the following upon termination of her employment"
        IF `the answer of s 76(5A)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "she forfeits her claim to any payment"
        IF `the answer of s 83` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the answer of s 76(1A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of the sections gathered answers
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The amount: the sum for the days (s 76(1A), s 77(1)), halved where s 80(3) limits her to half, and
-- nothing where the gathered rule says she is not entitled to any pay.
-- src:2807 | (1A) Subject to this section and section 77, every female employee
-- src:2808 | is entitled to receive payment from her employer at her gross rate of
-- src:2809 | pay for any of the following periods (called in this Part the benefit
-- src:2810 | period):
@ref s 76(1A) (src:2807-2810)
GIVEN `the answer of the gathered entitlement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 76(1A) the sum payable for the days of the benefit period` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the answer of s 80(3) she is entitled to only half` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 76(1A) gathered with s 80(3): the amount of the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of the gathered entitlement`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the answer of s 76(1A) the sum payable for the days of the benefit period`
        WHEN JUST sum THEN
            IF `the answer of s 80(3) she is entitled to only half` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST (sum DIVIDED BY 2)
            ELSE JUST sum
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the sum depends on the gross rate of pay for a day, which is not given
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of the sections gathered answers
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
